  "name": "Elusive",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p><em>You are, as a rule, not where the danger arrived expecting you. Blasts find the space you occupied a moment ago, grasping hands close on nothing, and the ground itself seems to decline to slow you down.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>1st Level</strong></p><ul><li>When you roll a Reflex save, improve the degree of success by one.</li><li>+5 feet to all Speeds, increasing by another 5 feet every 3 levels.</li><li>Your Move actions do not trigger reactions.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>5th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Move normally through difficult terrain.</li><li>Immune to Immobilized.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>10th Level</strong></p><ul><li>At the start of your turn, gain an extra action usable only for actions with the move trait.<ul><li>When you are Slowed, this extra action is lost first, and the Slowed value is reduced by 1 for determining how many of your remaining actions you lose.</li></ul></li><li>Move normally through greater difficult terrain.</li><li>Immune to Restrained.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Immune to Slowed.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>In Foundry:</strong> the Reflex improvement, the Speed increase (5 feet at 1st, another 5 at 4th, 7th, 10th, 13th, 16th and 19th) and the three immunities apply automatically.</p>\n<p>For the table: your Move actions not triggering reactions, moving normally through difficult and greater difficult terrain, and the extra move-only action from 10th level. PF2e has no hook for any of the three.</p>",
      "gm": ""
    },
